#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:144
msgid "Config Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:144
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:146
msgid "**DSN**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:146
msgid "The DSN connect string (an all-in-one configuration sequence)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:147
msgid "**hostname**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:147
msgid "The hostname of your database server. Often this is 'localhost'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:148
msgid "**username**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:148
msgid ""
"The username used to connect to the database. (``SQLite3`` does not use "
"this.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:149
msgid "**password**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:149
msgid ""
"The password used to connect to the database. (``SQLite3`` does not use "
"this.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:150
msgid "**database**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:150
msgid "The name of the database you want to connect to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:152
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter doesn't support dots (``.``) in the table and column names. "
"Since v4.5.0, database names with dots are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:154
msgid "**DBDriver**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:154
msgid ""
"The database driver name. The case must match the driver name. You can "
"set a fully qualified classname to use your custom driver. Supported "
"drivers: ``MySQLi``, ``Postgre``, ``SQLite3``, ``SQLSRV``, and ``OCI8``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:157
msgid "**DBPrefix**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:157
msgid ""
"An optional table prefix which will be added to the table name when "
"running :doc:`Query Builder <query_builder>` queries. This permits "
"multiple CodeIgniter installations to share one database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:160
msgid "**pConnect**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:160
msgid "true/false (boolean) - Whether to use a persistent connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:161
msgid "**DBDebug**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:161
msgid ""
"true/false (boolean) - Whether to throw exceptions when database errors "
"occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:162
msgid "**charset**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:162
msgid "The character set used in communicating with the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:163
msgid "**DBCollat**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:163
msgid ""
"(``MySQLi`` only) The character collation used in communicating with the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:164
msgid "**swapPre**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:164
msgid ""
"A default table prefix that should be swapped with ``DBPrefix``. This is "
"useful for distributed applications where you might run manually written "
"queries, and need the prefix to still be customizable by the end user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:167
msgid "**schema**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:167
msgid ""
"(``Postgre`` and ``SQLSRV`` only) The database schema, default value "
"varies by driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:168
msgid "**encrypt**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:168
msgid ""
"(``MySQLi`` and ``SQLSRV`` only) Whether to use an encrypted connection. "
"See :ref:`MySQLi encrypt <mysqli-encrypt>` for ``MySQLi`` settings. "
"``SQLSRV`` driver accepts true/false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:171
msgid "**compress**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:171
msgid "(``MySQLi`` only) Whether to use client compression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:172
msgid "**strictOn**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:172
msgid ""
"(``MySQLi`` only) true/false (boolean) - Whether to force \"Strict Mode\""
" connections, good for ensuring strict SQL while developing an "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:174
msgid "**port**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:174
msgid ""
"The database port number - Empty string ``''`` for default port (or "
"dynamic port with ``SQLSRV``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:175
msgid "**foreignKeys**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:175
msgid ""
"(``SQLite3`` only) true/false (boolean) - Whether to enable Foreign Key "
"constraint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:177
msgid ""
"SQLite3 Foreign Key constraint is disabled by default. See `SQLite "
"documentation <https://www.sqlite.org/pragma.html#pragma_foreign_keys>`_."
" To enforce Foreign Key constraint, set this config item to true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:180
msgid "**busyTimeout**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:180
msgid ""
"(``SQLite3`` only) milliseconds (int) - Sleeps for a specified amount of "
"time when a table is locked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:181
msgid "**synchronous**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:181
msgid ""
"(``SQLite3`` only) flag (int) - How strict SQLite will be at flushing to "
"disk during transactions. Use `null` to stay with the default setting. "
"This can be used since v4.6.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:183
msgid "**numberNative**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:183
msgid ""
"(``MySQLi`` only) true/false (boolean) - Whether to enable "
"MYSQLI_OPT_INT_AND_FLOAT_NATIVE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:184
msgid "**foundRows**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:184
msgid ""
"(``MySQLi`` only) true/false (boolean) - Whether to enable "
"MYSQLI_CLIENT_FOUND_ROWS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:185
msgid "**dateFormat**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:185
msgid ""
"The default date/time formats as PHP's `DateTime format`_. * ``date``"
"        - date format * ``datetime``    - date and time format * "
"``datetime-ms`` - date and time with millisecond format * ``datetime-us``"
" - date and time with microsecond format * ``time``        - time format "
"This can be used since v4.5.0, and you can get the value, e.g., "
"``$db->dateFormat['datetime']``. Currently, the database drivers do not "
"use these values directly, but :ref:`Model <model-saving-dates>` uses "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/configuration.rst:198
msgid ""
"Depending on what database driver you are using (``MySQLi``, ``Postgre``,"
" etc.) not all values will be needed. For example, when using ``SQLite3``"
" you will not need to supply a username or password, and the database "
"name will be the path to your database file."
msgstr ""

